  "id": "operant-behavior",
  "term": "operant behavior",
  "definition": "Operant behavior is behavior measured in an operant task, such as bar pressing while an animal self-administers a natural or drug reward. In this context, features of that responding, including how long a bar press lasts, can be used to detect psychological reactions to frustrating changes in reward conditions.",
